1
00:00:00,580 --> 00:00:04,139
The only ones who can enter
and leave this room are me,

2
00:00:04,140 --> 00:00:06,619
and those I allow.

3
00:00:06,620 --> 00:00:10,520
You understand, right, Snow White?

4
00:00:11,130 --> 00:00:14,449
The Magical Girl who passed
the exam without killing anyone,

5
00:00:14,450 --> 00:00:18,460
and buried the mastermind
along with her ambitions.

6
00:00:18,840 --> 00:00:22,290
I am only here to deliver
the Land of Magic's demands.

7
00:00:22,810 --> 00:00:24,810
Demands, huh?

8
00:00:25,250 --> 00:00:28,420
Release all the Magical Girls right now.

9
00:00:28,920 --> 00:00:32,180
I can consider it,
depending on the conditions.

10
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:34,280
What are your demands?

11
00:00:35,170 --> 00:00:38,099
Investigate all the
problematic exams of the past,

12
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:43,200
then revoke the Magical Girl status
of those who passed them.

13
00:00:43,850 --> 00:00:49,310
Your demands have already been rejected
by the Land of Magic's council.

14
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:50,799
Of course.

15
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:53,370
In that case,
I reject your demands as well.

16
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:59,079
The Land of Magic just doesn't want to
admit their own lack of oversight, right?

17
00:00:59,080 --> 00:01:02,889
I'm sick of that
play-it-safe attitude.

18
00:01:02,890 --> 00:01:06,769
Magical Girls are
beings chosen by God.

19
00:01:06,770 --> 00:01:10,639
There shouldn't be even
the slightest impurity.

20
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:13,609
Snow White! Six people
have already died, pon!

21
00:01:13,610 --> 00:01:14,640
We have to hurry...

22
00:01:16,250 --> 00:01:17,849
I will say it one more time.

23
00:01:17,850 --> 00:01:19,940
I'm sure you understand what I mean.

24
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:22,440
These negotiations are still ongoing.

25
00:01:23,160 --> 00:01:25,940
So, don't kill anyone else.

26
00:01:27,570 --> 00:01:30,459
I haven't killed anyone.

27
00:01:30,460 --> 00:01:32,739
I just gathered them
to play a game,

28
00:01:32,740 --> 00:01:34,860
and then they killed
each other on their own.

29
00:01:35,330 --> 00:01:40,059
This game was created so it could be
cleared by good and noble Magical Girls.

30
00:01:40,060 --> 00:01:43,129
What more could you ask of me as a Master?

31
00:01:43,130 --> 00:01:45,929
Instead of eliminating kids who became
Magical Girls through

32
00:01:45,930 --> 00:01:49,899
twisted means, I'm giving them a chance
to retake the exam through this game.

33
00:01:49,900 --> 00:01:52,689
Can you read my mind?

34
00:01:52,690 --> 00:01:55,800
I have absolutely no
blind spots here, you know.

35
00:01:56,220 --> 00:01:58,089
Just like God.

36
00:01:58,090 --> 00:02:01,859
You had a peer named
Nemurin in the past, didn't you?

37
00:02:01,860 --> 00:02:05,739
Just like her,
as long as I'm in this world,

38
00:02:05,740 --> 00:02:08,720
no one can touch me.

39
00:02:09,090 --> 00:02:14,160
Snow White, we can cooperate
and indeed we should cooperate.

40
00:02:14,700 --> 00:02:15,740
Right?

41
00:02:17,420 --> 00:02:23,000
Because both you and I
are true Magical Girls.

42
00:03:56,670 --> 00:04:00,970
EPISODE 7: NEGATIVES AND POSITIVES

43
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:16,359
The Recovery Potion! Hurry!

44
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:18,370
RECOVERY POTION
R-Right!

45
00:04:19,610 --> 00:04:20,860
ERROR: TARGET NOT DETECTED

46
00:04:26,700 --> 00:04:29,449
How are we supposed to
fight something like this?!

47
00:04:29,450 --> 00:04:32,180
Stop talking and focus!

48
00:04:54,190 --> 00:04:57,409
He noticed Clantail's
Dragon Slayer!

49
00:04:57,410 --> 00:04:58,330
Watch out!

50
00:04:58,740 --> 00:04:59,660
Why?!

51
00:05:01,280 --> 00:05:03,530
Run, Clantail-san!

52
00:05:20,370 --> 00:05:22,279
Pfu-cchi was right.

53
00:05:22,280 --> 00:05:25,710
Leaving a gem with Tail-cchi
was the right move!

54
00:05:27,240 --> 00:05:28,600
Checkmate.

55
00:05:45,520 --> 00:05:47,279
I'm so exhausted!

56
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:49,500
Are you okay, Lazuline?!

57
00:05:55,730 --> 00:05:57,569
F-Finally we...

58
00:05:57,570 --> 00:05:59,500
We managed to defeat it.

59
00:06:06,360 --> 00:06:07,959
Up ahead...

60
00:06:07,960 --> 00:06:10,020
The next Area!

61
00:06:13,130 --> 00:06:14,330
What is it?

62
00:06:18,380 --> 00:06:20,330
No way...

63
00:06:23,240 --> 00:06:25,340
How were the results, Detective-san?

64
00:06:26,140 --> 00:06:31,200
What was the meaning behind
Genopsyko's actions back then?

65
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:36,579
The direct cause of @Meow-Meow's death
was indeed the Great Dragon's fire.

66
00:06:36,580 --> 00:06:40,849
But the one who triggered
the attack was clearly Genopsyko.

67
00:06:40,850 --> 00:06:45,720
@Meow-Meow was murdered
by Yumenoshima Genopsyko.

68
00:06:46,040 --> 00:06:49,549
Could Genopsyko have been tailing us?

69
00:06:49,550 --> 00:06:54,739
If she had been tailing us,
she would have heard what I said too.

70
00:06:54,740 --> 00:06:56,299
Then,

71
00:06:56,300 --> 00:07:00,569
she wouldn't have left
her suit's visor open.

72
00:07:00,570 --> 00:07:03,170
Did she want to take her down with her?

73
00:07:04,300 --> 00:07:08,179
If the traitor really was @Meow-Meow...

74
00:07:08,180 --> 00:07:09,249
Wait.

75
00:07:09,250 --> 00:07:12,700
Besides, why would she sacrifice herself?

76
00:07:13,280 --> 00:07:14,680
Detec Bell.

77
00:07:15,810 --> 00:07:20,430
Even your magic couldn't
find any clues, huh?

78
00:07:21,180 --> 00:07:24,800
I've investigated everything
that needed to be checked.

79
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:26,500
I see.

80
00:07:27,140 --> 00:07:28,270
Thank you.

81
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:40,310
Nokkochan...

82
00:07:41,300 --> 00:07:43,899
I have the most physical strength,

83
00:07:43,900 --> 00:07:45,879
so let me dig the grave.

84
00:07:45,880 --> 00:07:48,740
No, let me do it.

85
00:07:49,170 --> 00:07:51,299
But doing it alone...

86
00:07:51,300 --> 00:07:52,780
This is my responsibility.

87
00:07:54,610 --> 00:07:56,030
Wait a moment.

88
00:07:57,890 --> 00:07:58,870
Here...

89
00:08:01,500 --> 00:08:03,040
A shovel?

90
00:08:03,330 --> 00:08:05,060
Use this.

91
00:08:05,620 --> 00:08:07,700
Thank you very much.

92
00:08:40,490 --> 00:08:42,359
They're all empty.

93
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:44,060
Not interesting at all.

94
00:08:47,450 --> 00:08:49,699
All alone in a place like that...

95
00:08:49,700 --> 00:08:52,649
Just to be killed like that...

96
00:08:52,650 --> 00:08:56,930
There's no need to pity the Great Dragon.

97
00:08:57,720 --> 00:09:00,199
Please stop reading my mind.

98
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:04,020
We've known each other for
a long time, this is a trivial matter.

99
00:09:04,460 --> 00:09:05,720
For example...

100
00:09:06,050 --> 00:09:10,049
You definitely think of me
as an old man, right?

101
00:09:10,050 --> 00:09:12,619
That's because you really
are like an old man, Miss.

102
00:09:12,620 --> 00:09:14,299
Draining your allowance

103
00:09:14,300 --> 00:09:18,479
to hunt for comfortable chairs
on online shopping sites?

104
00:09:18,480 --> 00:09:22,050
That's more like an old person's taste
than a young person's, right?

105
00:09:23,640 --> 00:09:25,770
None of your business, Miss.

106
00:09:26,100 --> 00:09:27,619
If you keep that up,

107
00:09:27,620 --> 00:09:32,120
I doubt you can complete
the task I give you later.

108
00:09:33,460 --> 00:09:35,770
What is your order?

109
00:09:36,060 --> 00:09:37,769
Just a normal task.

110
00:09:37,770 --> 00:09:40,139
Open the item guidebook.

111
00:09:40,140 --> 00:09:43,400
Check what can be bought in this area.

112
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:48,410
It's pretty convenient that it stays
listed even if another party buys it.

113
00:09:48,820 --> 00:09:51,679
The Magic Board we bought.

114
00:09:51,680 --> 00:09:55,860
One-person capacity, speed is
equivalent to an adult man's sprint.

115
00:09:56,770 --> 00:09:58,609
Holy Charm.

116
00:09:58,610 --> 00:10:01,319
Grants holy element to the user,

117
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:04,479
increasing defense against evil monsters.

118
00:10:04,480 --> 00:10:06,670
While also increasing attack power.

119
00:10:07,200 --> 00:10:10,060
Another party bought this too.

120
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:13,199
Weapon +7, Shield +7.

121
00:10:13,200 --> 00:10:16,440
The effects are certainly great,
but they are incredibly expensive.

122
00:10:16,760 --> 00:10:18,729
To get those items,

123
00:10:18,730 --> 00:10:23,939
it seems many parties almost
exhausted all their Magical Candies.

124
00:10:23,940 --> 00:10:27,189
The Random Items obtained so far,

125
00:10:27,190 --> 00:10:29,579
including those of other parties,

126
00:10:29,580 --> 00:10:33,339
are maps, toothbrush sets, toy bows,

127
00:10:33,340 --> 00:10:35,210
rock climbing ropes...

128
00:10:36,880 --> 00:10:39,720
They're all everyday items, huh.

129
00:10:40,980 --> 00:10:43,830
But this one seems interesting.

130
00:10:44,360 --> 00:10:47,119
Starting Position Changer.

131
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:52,840
Allows us to choose our starting
area when the game begins.

132
00:10:53,930 --> 00:10:57,840
Whether it's interesting or not,
this item is certainly practical.

133
00:10:58,380 --> 00:10:59,929
Dragon Shield.

134
00:10:59,930 --> 00:11:02,939
This is the item drop
from the Great Dragon.

135
00:11:02,940 --> 00:11:05,659
A shield equivalent to +12.

136
00:11:05,660 --> 00:11:08,060
This item will be the key.

137
00:11:09,240 --> 00:11:10,870
Back then...

138
00:11:11,360 --> 00:11:14,019
I want the area unlock reward

139
00:11:14,020 --> 00:11:18,490
and all the Candy rewards to be mine.

140
00:11:21,320 --> 00:11:25,639
You said those outrageous things
on purpose just to get this, didn't you?

141
00:11:25,640 --> 00:11:30,459
If I act greedy from the start, they'll
be willing to give up the item drop.

142
00:11:30,460 --> 00:11:32,969
Isn't that right?

143
00:11:32,970 --> 00:11:36,459
Truly, when it comes
to cunning tricks like this,

144
00:11:36,460 --> 00:11:39,110
you are a genius, Miss.

145
00:11:39,700 --> 00:11:43,359
Now, onto the next plan.

146
00:11:43,360 --> 00:11:45,979
Can I ask one thing?

147
00:11:45,980 --> 00:11:47,240
Go ahead.

148
00:11:47,820 --> 00:11:51,580
Was the traitor really @Meow-Meow?

149
00:11:52,490 --> 00:11:56,130
Or at least, did Genopsyko think so?

150
00:11:56,560 --> 00:12:01,020
Even so, she didn't need to go
as far as dying along with her.

151
00:12:01,820 --> 00:12:04,889
Regardless of what Genopsyko's plan was.

152
00:12:04,890 --> 00:12:07,119
Even though @Meow-Meow is dead,

153
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:09,969
the Miracle Coin is still
in someone's phone.

154
00:12:09,970 --> 00:12:13,859
That means Masked Wonder's killer

155
00:12:13,860 --> 00:12:17,389
is still participating in this game.

156
00:12:17,390 --> 00:12:19,400
Can I ask one more thing?

157
00:12:19,920 --> 00:12:21,219
What is it?

158
00:12:21,220 --> 00:12:23,879
To defeat the Great Dragon,

159
00:12:23,880 --> 00:12:27,980
was it really necessary
to gather that many people?

160
00:12:28,300 --> 00:12:31,499
Have you forgotten
that death match?

161
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:35,740
We were only able to defeat it
after utilizing all our strength.

162
00:12:37,140 --> 00:12:40,759
Besides, considering
your personality, Miss,

163
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:43,489
there's no way you planned
to cooperate with everyone.

164
00:12:43,490 --> 00:12:46,659
By deliberately creating that situation,

165
00:12:46,660 --> 00:12:49,110
you must be after something.

166
00:12:49,620 --> 00:12:54,200
If so, @Meow-Meow's death
is partly your doing, Miss.

167
00:12:54,720 --> 00:12:58,299
From the beginning, you never
hesitated to do this kind of thing.

168
00:12:58,300 --> 00:12:59,990
Because you are a "bad person".

169
00:13:00,740 --> 00:13:03,340
I have a good idea.

170
00:13:04,100 --> 00:13:05,360
W-What is it?

171
00:13:06,080 --> 00:13:08,370
Let's disband this party.

172
00:13:11,020 --> 00:13:12,270
What?

173
00:13:18,360 --> 00:13:19,529
The enemy has appeared!

174
00:13:19,530 --> 00:13:23,160
Have you all equipped
your Holy Charms?

175
00:13:23,490 --> 00:13:25,170
Of course!

176
00:13:30,840 --> 00:13:32,919
Cool...

177
00:13:32,920 --> 00:13:34,420
Justice!

178
00:13:57,170 --> 00:14:01,919
So if we sit in the chairs,
they can't see us, huh.

179
00:14:01,920 --> 00:14:04,190
Thank goodness.

180
00:14:11,070 --> 00:14:13,580
THE DEMON KING IS STRONG

181
00:14:14,410 --> 00:14:16,540
Pechka-san, what is it?

182
00:14:16,850 --> 00:14:19,550
We received a message.

183
00:14:23,770 --> 00:14:26,619
I wonder if the Demon King
is really strong?

184
00:14:26,620 --> 00:14:29,919
There's no way
the final boss isn't strong.

185
00:14:29,920 --> 00:14:32,780
There's no point in thinking about it.

186
00:14:33,280 --> 00:14:35,299
Thank you for the meal.

187
00:14:35,300 --> 00:14:36,879
It's delicious.

188
00:14:36,880 --> 00:14:39,019
Pechka-san is really the best!

189
00:14:39,020 --> 00:14:43,639
Having a reward like this makes pushing
through those sweaty battles worth it.

190
00:14:43,640 --> 00:14:46,139
I completely agree with that!

191
00:14:46,140 --> 00:14:47,782
Her cooking is incredibly delicious.

192
00:14:49,890 --> 00:14:52,040
Thank you very much.

193
00:14:54,370 --> 00:14:57,240
Rionetta-san? What's wrong?

194
00:14:57,860 --> 00:15:04,050
In the real world, I have
a hard time getting good food.

195
00:15:04,410 --> 00:15:07,889
Every day my life is
barely enough just to survive.

196
00:15:07,890 --> 00:15:10,509
Being able to enjoy
Pechka-san's cooking

197
00:15:10,510 --> 00:15:13,830
is the happiest moment for me.

198
00:15:15,900 --> 00:15:19,360
Hearing you say that
makes me really happy.

199
00:15:21,130 --> 00:15:24,729
Come on, let's find
a new hunting ground!

200
00:15:24,730 --> 00:15:26,580
Ah, okay.

201
00:15:30,580 --> 00:15:34,289
The logout event is about to begin, pon.

202
00:15:34,290 --> 00:15:37,050
Oh my, is it already time?

203
00:15:37,410 --> 00:15:42,050
All players, please gather at
the plaza in the Barren Area, pon.

204
00:15:42,610 --> 00:15:46,280
What do we have to do this time?

205
00:15:55,430 --> 00:15:57,849
I wonder what's next?

206
00:15:57,850 --> 00:15:59,471
Considering what happened before...

207
00:16:00,140 --> 00:16:01,939
we can't let our guard down.

208
00:16:01,940 --> 00:16:05,459
That person is usually with Pfle...

209
00:16:05,460 --> 00:16:10,129
It seems Pfle-san joined
Bell-san's party.

210
00:16:10,130 --> 00:16:11,219
Eh?

211
00:16:11,220 --> 00:16:13,209
They probably just had a fight, right?

212
00:16:13,210 --> 00:16:15,040
That's a normal occurrence.

213
00:16:15,360 --> 00:16:17,289
Everyone has gathered, pon.

214
00:16:17,290 --> 00:16:21,200
The pre-maintenance event this time is...

215
00:16:21,740 --> 00:16:23,800
Rock-paper-scissors, pon!

216
00:16:24,250 --> 00:16:25,339
What?

217
00:16:25,340 --> 00:16:27,850
Rock-paper-scissors?!

218
00:16:28,170 --> 00:16:32,049
What's the penalty
for losing?

219
00:16:32,050 --> 00:16:34,009
There is no penalty, pon.

220
00:16:34,010 --> 00:16:35,969
Whoever wins until the end,

221
00:16:35,970 --> 00:16:39,819
will be rewarded with
1.000 Magical Candies, pon.

222
00:16:39,820 --> 00:16:40,630
1.000?!

223
00:16:41,060 --> 00:16:43,199
1.000 Candies is a lot!

224
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:46,659
There's an item you're aiming for,
but you don't have enough Candies.

225
00:16:46,660 --> 00:16:49,729
Things like that
must happen often, pon.

226
00:16:49,730 --> 00:16:53,700
Especially if the distribution rate
of the item is very low, pon.

227
00:16:54,160 --> 00:16:56,889
Collect as many Candies as possible,

228
00:16:56,890 --> 00:17:02,200
then get the item you want
before the other players, pon.

229
00:17:03,020 --> 00:17:08,219
It would be even better if item ownership
could be decided peacefully, pon.

230
00:17:08,220 --> 00:17:10,640
How can you say that now.

231
00:17:13,640 --> 00:17:16,409
Rock, paper, scissors, pon!

232
00:17:16,410 --> 00:17:19,099
Again, pon!

233
00:17:19,100 --> 00:17:21,419
Aw, I lost!

234
00:17:21,420 --> 00:17:22,700
Sorry.

235
00:17:23,050 --> 00:17:24,819
That's a shame.

236
00:17:24,820 --> 00:17:27,129
Even though Nokkochan
survived for a long time.

237
00:17:27,130 --> 00:17:28,699
It can't be helped.

238
00:17:28,700 --> 00:17:31,820
You were accepted into
Bell-san's party, huh.

239
00:17:33,410 --> 00:17:36,580
Since I was the only one left...

240
00:17:37,220 --> 00:17:38,840
I see.

241
00:17:39,580 --> 00:17:41,579
That's true.

242
00:17:41,580 --> 00:17:46,390
Even though she acts normal,
it must be hard on her.

243
00:17:47,340 --> 00:17:48,969
Amazing.

244
00:17:48,970 --> 00:17:51,830
You can even win
rock-paper-scissors so effortlessly.

245
00:17:52,180 --> 00:17:53,689
It was just a coincidence.

246
00:17:53,690 --> 00:17:55,660
Can I ask you one thing?

247
00:17:56,060 --> 00:17:57,360
About what?

248
00:17:57,740 --> 00:17:59,859
I'll just ask straight away.

249
00:17:59,860 --> 00:18:01,649
What happened to you two?

250
00:18:01,650 --> 00:18:04,839
Shadow Gale and I
had a difference of opinion,

251
00:18:04,840 --> 00:18:07,409
so we decided to part ways.

252
00:18:07,410 --> 00:18:09,170
Sorry for troubling you.

253
00:18:09,560 --> 00:18:13,170
If that's the reason,
we don't mind...

254
00:18:13,460 --> 00:18:16,659
That is all for this event, pon.

255
00:18:16,660 --> 00:18:18,870
It is time to logout, pon.

256
00:18:48,930 --> 00:18:53,550
I am always in my Magical Girl form.

257
00:18:54,400 --> 00:18:55,760
The reason is...

258
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:00,890
Be careful, Noriko-chan.

259
00:19:01,700 --> 00:19:03,030
I'm off.

260
00:19:03,480 --> 00:19:05,369
With magic,

261
00:19:05,370 --> 00:19:09,179
a child living alone won't be
considered weird by anyone.

262
00:19:09,180 --> 00:19:10,889
That's why...

263
00:19:10,890 --> 00:19:13,380
MANABEGAWA 3RD PUBLIC ELEMENTARY SCHOOL

264
00:19:14,060 --> 00:19:16,329
CLASS 4-2
They said during the cultural festival

265
00:19:16,330 --> 00:19:18,479
CLASS 4-2
yesterday, our class was the best.

266
00:19:18,480 --> 00:19:20,529
CLASS 4-2
Sensei is also happy for you.

267
00:19:20,530 --> 00:19:24,289
That's because Noguchi-sensei
helped us too.

268
00:19:24,290 --> 00:19:27,680
My class, Class 4-2, is a good class.

269
00:19:28,270 --> 00:19:31,609
Everyone works hard
and has fun together.

270
00:19:31,610 --> 00:19:34,279
Of course, no one bullies the weak.

271
00:19:34,280 --> 00:19:37,339
Let's work hard together again
at the upcoming sports festival.

272
00:19:37,340 --> 00:19:39,260
Okay!

273
00:19:40,290 --> 00:19:45,729
Our homeroom teacher, Noguchi-sensei,
used to yell at the students.

274
00:19:45,730 --> 00:19:48,230
But now he never yells anymore.

275
00:19:49,460 --> 00:19:51,739
The classroom feels
so cheerful and pleasant.

276
00:19:51,740 --> 00:19:56,679
Also, no one cares
even if I stay in this form.

277
00:19:56,680 --> 00:20:00,680
CLASS 4-2

278
00:20:02,690 --> 00:20:04,859
I told you I was first!

279
00:20:04,860 --> 00:20:06,940
Give it back to me!

280
00:20:07,400 --> 00:20:10,449
What are you talking about?!
I got it first, you know!

281
00:20:10,450 --> 00:20:12,639
You already played with it earlier!

282
00:20:12,640 --> 00:20:14,519
You always play with it yourself!

283
00:20:14,520 --> 00:20:16,019
Shut up!

284
00:20:16,020 --> 00:20:17,620
Let go!

285
00:20:21,330 --> 00:20:23,269
Fine, I'll just play with it later.

286
00:20:23,270 --> 00:20:25,900
But you got to it first anyway.

287
00:20:26,320 --> 00:20:27,440
I'm sorry.

288
00:20:30,120 --> 00:20:32,319
PEDESTRIANS AND BICYCLES ONLY
When someone is upset,

289
00:20:32,320 --> 00:20:35,390
PEDESTRIANS AND BICYCLES ONLY
I can amplify their feelings of happiness.

290
00:20:36,200 --> 00:20:38,219
PEDESTRIANS AND BICYCLES ONLY
When someone is sad,

291
00:20:38,220 --> 00:20:40,600
PEDESTRIANS AND BICYCLES ONLY
I can soothe their sadness.

292
00:20:41,200 --> 00:20:44,100
Because that is my magic.

293
00:20:45,810 --> 00:20:47,599
ISHIKAWA GENERAL HOSPITAL
Wow, visiting again today?

294
00:20:47,600 --> 00:20:49,049
ISHIKAWA GENERAL HOSPITAL
Such a diligent child.

295
00:20:49,050 --> 00:20:49,899
ISHIKAWA GENERAL HOSPITAL
Yes.

296
00:20:49,900 --> 00:20:51,860
ISHIKAWA GENERAL HOSPITAL
Thank you for taking care of my mother.

297
00:20:53,860 --> 00:20:55,220
Mom.

298
00:20:55,870 --> 00:20:57,219
I'm here.

299
00:20:57,220 --> 00:20:59,359
Welcome, Noriko.

300
00:20:59,360 --> 00:21:00,839
Sorry to make you come here every day.

301
00:21:00,840 --> 00:21:03,380
It's okay.

302
00:21:04,330 --> 00:21:09,380
During the cultural festival yesterday,
sensei said our class was the best.

303
00:21:10,040 --> 00:21:13,460
I'm sorry I couldn't come.

304
00:21:16,520 --> 00:21:18,740
It's fine.

305
00:21:28,970 --> 00:21:32,099
After all, I've already seen
plenty of your photos.

306
00:21:32,100 --> 00:21:33,140
Yeah.

307
00:21:36,540 --> 00:21:39,279
Mom didn't say anything.

308
00:21:39,280 --> 00:21:41,149
Mom's hospital bills are very expensive

309
00:21:41,150 --> 00:21:43,160
and we can't afford the surgery.

310
00:21:43,840 --> 00:21:45,739
With the magic I have,

311
00:21:45,740 --> 00:21:49,750
I can only make Mom feel more cheerful.

312
00:21:55,380 --> 00:21:56,699
I see.

313
00:21:56,700 --> 00:22:00,910
It seems the clear reward is divided
equally by the number of players.

314
00:22:02,480 --> 00:22:06,430
Alright, I'd better get changed
and fold the laundry.

315
00:23:40,020 --> 00:23:49,980
LAZULINE'S DREAM

